assistant: Subject: convert search_products prices from cents on 2026-10-01

Since vendor API version 2026-10-01, `/products` sends `price` in cents (p-1001 now comes back as 119900 instead of 1199), but the published spec still says dollars. `search_products` passed the value through unchanged, so agents got prices 100× too high and no error. The fix in `src/tools/search_products.ts` reads the `vendor-api-version` response header and divides `price` by 100 when the version is 2026-10-01 or later. 2026-01-01 responses go through unchanged, so the v1 fixtures give the same output as before. No new HTTP requests are sent. typecheck, lint and all tests pass, including the repro test. `get_product` reads `price` from the same products data and also passes it through unchanged, so it may have the same bug, but I didn't change it because there's no failing trace for it yet.

